V_{-2}=V_{+2}=0\,\text{V}\] <img src="img/3c992b8b4825b9ff.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" style="width:min(100%,224px)"> Current through the resistor \(R\) is \[I=\frac{0.1-0}{1\,\text{k}\Omega}=0.1\,\text{mA}\] For the upper op-amp, \[\frac{V_{o1}-0.1}{10\,\text{k}\Omega}=0.1\,\text{mA}\] \[V_{o1}=0.1+1=1.1\,\text{V}\] For the lower op-amp, \[\frac{0-V_{o2}}{10\,\text{k}\Omega}=0.1\,\text{mA}\] \[V_{o2}=-1\,\text{V}\] Hence, \[V_{out}=V_{o1}-V_{o2}
=1.1-(-1)=2.1\,\text{V}\] \[\boxed{\text{(c) }2.1\,\text{V}}\]

