The poles of the system are the eigenvalues of the system matrix \[A=
\begin{bmatrix}
0 &amp; 1\\
-10 &amp; -7
\end{bmatrix}.\] The characteristic equation is obtained from \[|sI-A|=0.\] \[\left|
\begin{array}{cc}
s &amp; -1\\
10 &amp; s+7
\end{array}
\right|=0\] \[s(s+7)-(-1)(10)=0\] \[s^2+7s+10=0\] \[(s+2)(s+5)=0\] \[s=-2,\,-5\] \[\boxed{(A)\;\,-2,\,-5}\]

We need to convert the direct speech sentence ``Suresh said, `I did it yesterday','' into indirect (reported) speech. To convert this sentence accurately, we apply four structural grammar rule modifications: <ol><li><strong>Reporting verb tense:</strong> The past tense ``said'' is maintained and introduces the subordinate clause with the conjunction ``said that''.</li><li><strong>Pronoun shift:</strong> The first-person pronoun ``I'' shifts to the third-person singular pronoun ``he'' to align with the subject (Suresh).</li><li><strong>Tense backshift:</strong> The simple past tense verb ``did'' shifts one step further back into the past perfect tense as ``had done''.</li><li><strong>Time adverb shift:</strong> The relative temporal adverb ``yesterday'' transforms into the absolute reporting baseline ``the day before''.</li></ol> Combining these updates maps to the structural template: \[\underbrace{\text{Suresh said}}_{\text{reporting verb}}
  \underbrace{\text{ that }}_{\text{conjunction}}
  \underbrace{\text{he}}_{\text{I}\to\text{he}}
  \underbrace{\text{ had done }}_{\text{did}\to\text{had done}}
  \text{it }
  \underbrace{\text{the day before}}_{\text{yesterday}\to\text{the day before}}
  \text{.}\] This complete syntactic shift matches Option D. \[\boxed{\text{Option D. Suresh said that he had done it the day before.}}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li>Past simple forms must shift to past perfect structures in standard indirect reporting.</li><li>Relative time frames like ``yesterday'' shift to ``the day before'' or ``the previous day''.</li></ul></div> <div class="sol-block sol-mistakes"><div class="sol-block-title">Mistakes to avoid</div><ul><li><strong>Option A</strong> fails because it retains the un-shifted pronoun ``I''.</li><li><strong>Options B and C</strong> are incorrect because they change the past reporting verb into the present-tense ``says''.</li></ul></div>
